				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				342,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Add SkyEvent registry for Mountain → Wind Tauri events\n\nMountain emits Tauri events on `sky://…` URIs to notify the webview of\nstate changes that don't originate from a Wind-initiated `invoke` call.\nHistorically each emit site used a free-text string literal and each Wind\nlistener matched against its own free-text string — drift was invisible\nuntil runtime (the listener simply never fired).\n\n`SkyEvent` provides the single source of truth, following the same\n`DefineSkyEvents!` macro pattern established for `Channel`. The enum\nproduces wire strings via `AsStr()` and parses them via `FromStr`, with\n~100 events covering Configuration, Debug, Diagnostics, Dialog, Documents,\nEditor, Extensions, ExtHost, Input, Language, Lifecycle, Native,\nNotifications, Output, Progress, QuickPick, SCM, Status bar, Task, Terminal,\nTest, Theme, Tree view, UI, VFS, Webview, Window, and Workspace.\n\nThis change also adds 3 legacy channels to Channel.rs that predate the\n`prefix:method` convention: `MountainGetStatus` (snake_case) and the\n`UserInterface.Show*Dialog` dotted names from the original Cocoon→Mountain\ngRPC protocol.\n\nThe matching TypeScript const object lives at Element/Wind/Source/IPC/SkyEvent.ts,\nkept in sync by convention. This eliminates silent runtime failures from typos\nin event names and enables compile-time verification of the event namespace.",
			"SHA": "7063d00c816177a4b01b30eec72e5a90218ea498"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:09:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				341,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Add QuickInput, TextFile, and WorkingCopy IPC channels\n\nExtend the IPC Channel registry with 9 new channel definitions across three categories needed for Wind ↔ Mountain communication:\n\n- QuickInput: showInputBox and showQuickPick for VS Code-style dialogs\n- TextFile: read, write, and save operations for the editor's working-copy surface\n- WorkingCopy: getAllDirty, getDirtyCount, isDirty, and setDirty for dirty-state tracking\n\nThese channels complete the IPC contract for the text editor and quick input services, enabling the Wind frontend to invoke these backend operations via Tauri invoke calls.",
			"SHA": "da495acc37a803d18c29fc76dba7b31caba6d3b5"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1782484750517
}